[[File:Parsnik (Beta 41.0).png|thumb|294x294px|Beta 41.0]]
Parsnik changed a few times, but never too heavily. Its first change was during '''Beta 4.8''', in which its ATK dropped from 4 to 3. Much later, in '''Beta 26.0''', its Magic effect was buffed by not just paralyzing an enemy monster, but also dealing 2 DMG to it when it's paralyzed, getting similar changes as [https://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Cold_Winter Cold Winter]. '''Beta 31.0''' increased its ranged to be able to affect ally monsters. This was reverted the next day in '''Beta 31.1'''.
[[File:Parsnik (Beta 49.1).png|thumb|291x291px|Beta 49.1]]
'''Beta 41.0''' made it no longer re-paralyze paralyzed monsters (something it also shares with Cold Winter and something that was made impossible to do entirely as of Beta 42.0). '''Beta 49.1''' reduced its HP from 4 to/by 2. [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Ponman Dark Ponman] was reworked in this update, and Parsnik received its old effect. If Parsnik is played on the left side of the board (slot 1 or 2), it will still Paralyze an enemy monster of your choice (though no longer deal DMG if it's already paralyzed). But if played on the right (slot 3 or 4), the targeted enemy monster will now be Silenced instead. '''Beta 52.0''' reverted it back to its Beta 31.0 version (but without the consecutive Paralysis), being at 4 HP and able to Paralyze any monster.
